<section class="page-hero compact-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Trust protocol</span><h1>Privacy at the <span class="gradient-text">Nexus</span></h1><p>Clear information about the data used to operate your account and reservations.</p></div></section>
<section class="section-space pt-4"><div class="container form-container"><div class="neon-form"><h2>What we store</h2><p class="text-secondary">Neon Nexus stores your display name, email address, optional phone number, and reservation history. Passwords are protected by ASP.NET Core Identity and are never stored as plain text.</p><hr /><h2>Why we use it</h2><p class="text-secondary">Account information identifies your reservations, helps staff support your visit, and prevents unauthorized access to another customer's booking history.</p><hr /><h2>Security</h2><p class="text-secondary">The application uses secure authentication cookies, server-side authorization, anti-forgery protection, validation, and ownership checks. This portfolio version does not process or store payment card information.</p><hr /><h2>Development notice</h2><p class="text-secondary mb-0">This is a portfolio demonstration running on a development database. Configure a production privacy policy, retention period, email confirmation, and operational contact before a public launch.</p></div></div></section>
